/*
 * LC 525 — Contiguous Array
 *
 * PROBLEM:
 * Given binary array (0s and 1s), find length of longest subarray
 * with equal number of 0s and 1s.
 *
 * ════════════════════════════════════════════════
 * THE THEORY — STEP BY STEP IN SIMPLE WORDS
 * ════════════════════════════════════════════════
 *
 * STEP 1 — TRANSFORM THE PROBLEM
 * Replace every 0 with -1.
 * Now "equal 0s and 1s" becomes "subarray sum equals 0".
 * Because: each 0 contributes -1, each 1 contributes +1.
 * Equal count → they cancel out → sum = 0.
 *
 * Example:
 *   nums     = [0,  1,  0,  1]
 *   replaced = [-1, 1, -1,  1]
 *   equal 0s and 1s → sum = 0 ✅
 *
 * STEP 2 — THE KEY INSIGHT (why HashMap needed)
 * Track running sum (prefix sum) as we iterate.
 * THE MAGIC RULE:
 *   If the same prefix sum appears at two different indices i and j,
 *   then the subarray BETWEEN them sums to 0.
 *
 * Why? If sum is same at both points, nothing net was added between them.
 *   prefixSum[i] == prefixSum[j]
 *   → elements between i+1 and j cancel out
 *   → that subarray has equal 0s and 1s
 *   → length = j - i
 *
 * STEP 3 — WHY WE STORE ALL SUMS, NOT JUST WHEN SUM=0
 * Beginners think: "just check when running sum becomes 0".
 * That ONLY catches subarrays starting from index 0.
 * It MISSES subarrays in the middle.
 *
 * Example where sum NEVER hits 0:
 *   replaced = [-1, -1, 1, -1, -1, -1, 1, 1]
 *   prefixSums: -1,-2,-1,-2,-3,-4,-3,-2
 *   Sum never equals 0!
 *   BUT prefixSum=-2 appears at index 1 and index 7
 *   → subarray from index 2 to 7 sums to 0 → length 6 ✅
 *   Checking only "sum==0" would return 0 — completely wrong!
 *
 * This is why we store EVERY prefix sum in the HashMap.
 *
 * STEP 4 — WHAT THE HASHMAP STORES
 *   map: prefixSum → FIRST index where this sum appeared
 *
 * WHY FIRST index (never update if already present):
 *   We want the LONGEST subarray → largest (j - i)
 *   → we need the SMALLEST i (earliest occurrence)
 *   → so store first time only, never overwrite
 *
 * STEP 5 — THE BASE CASE {0 → -1}
 * We initialize map with prefixSum=0 at index -1.
 * This represents "sum of 0 exists before the array starts".
 * It handles subarrays that start from index 0:
 *   If prefixSum at index j = 0
 *   → length = j - (-1) = j + 1
 *   → entire subarray from 0 to j counted correctly ✅
 *
 * ════════════════════════════════════════════════
 * THE ALGORITHM
 * ════════════════════════════════════════════════
 * 1. Replace all 0 with -1
 * 2. Initialize map = {0 → -1}, sum = 0, maxLen = 0
 * 3. For each index i:
 *    a. sum += nums[i]
 *    b. if sum already in map:
 *         length = i - map.get(sum)
 *         maxLen = max(maxLen, length)
 *       else:
 *         map.put(sum, i)   ← store first occurrence only
 * 4. Return maxLen
 *
 * ════════════════════════════════════════════════
 * COMPARISON WITH RELATED PROBLEMS
 * ════════════════════════════════════════════════
 * ┌──────────────┬────────────────┬───────────────────┬──────────────────┐
 * │              │ LC 560         │ LC 525            │ Longest Sum K    │
 * ├──────────────┼────────────────┼───────────────────┼──────────────────┤
 * │ Goal         │ count subarrays│ longest subarray  │ longest subarray │
 * │ Map stores   │ sum→frequency  │ sum→first index   │ sum→first index  │
 * │ Map update   │ always update  │ only if absent    │ only if absent   │
 * │ Result       │ count+=freq    │ max(i-firstIdx)   │ max(i-firstIdx)  │
 * └──────────────┴────────────────┴───────────────────┴──────────────────┘
 *
 * RULE OF THUMB:
 * - Counting subarrays → store frequency, always update
 * - Longest/shortest subarray → store first index, never update
 *
 * ════════════════════════════════════════════════
 * COMPLEXITY
 * ════════════════════════════════════════════════
 * TC: O(n) — single pass, O(1) map operations
 * SC: O(n) — map stores at most n distinct prefix sums
 *
 * Edge cases:
 * - All same (e.g. [0,0,0]) → no equal subarray → return 0
 * - [0,1] → sum hits 0 at index 1 → length 2 ✅
 * - Sum never hits 0 but repeats → caught by HashMap ✅
 */
public int findMaxLength(int[] nums) {
    // step 1 — replace 0 with -1 so equal 0s/1s becomes sum=0
    for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++)
        if (nums[i] == 0) nums[i] = -1;

    Map<Integer, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
    map.put(0, -1); // base case — sum 0 exists before array starts
    int sum = 0, maxLen = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
        sum += nums[i];
        if (map.containsKey(sum)) {
            // same prefix sum seen before → subarray between sums to 0
            maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, i - map.get(sum));
        } else {
            // store FIRST occurrence only — never update (want longest)
            map.put(sum, i);
        }
    }
    return maxLen;
}
